  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Portfolio Website**\n\nI\'m focusing on crafting a high-end light theme portfolio website. The initial decisions point to a React stack with Vite, Tailwind CSS, and Motion. We\'re aiming for a visual style that\'s modern and Apple/Stripe inspired, with smooth, engaging animations. We are building the initial components.\n\n\n**Refining Project Structure**\n\nI\'ve decided to proceed with React components within the Vite setup, despite the initial mention of separate HTML/CSS/JS files, since that is now how the AI Studio project is configured. Tailwind and Framer Motion will be used for visuals, animations and the style. The components will now be implemented with TSX, as it\'s the more ideal. This aligns better with the desired \"Apple/Stripe inspired\" aesthetics, and I\'ll adapt to the project environment. I\'m focusing on a clean React component structure. I will address deployment later.\n\n\n**Outlining Key Website Sections**\n\nI\'m now outlining the key sections for the portfolio site, from Hero to Footer, including About, Services, Projects (with a dynamic grid), Skills, and Contact. I\'ll use `lucide-react` for icons and `framer-motion` for animations, styled with Tailwind CSS in a light theme with gradients and soft shadows. Inter will be the primary typography. I will start by modifying `App.tsx` and adding the basic components. I am refining the color scheme using grey background and accents with gradient text. I will create a clean file structure.\n\n\n**Structuring Component Files**\n\nI\'m now establishing a component directory structure with separate files for About, Services, Process, Projects, Skills, Achievements, Certifications, Contact, and Footer, all in the src/components/ directory. This is for maintainability, and aligns well with the React setup. I\'ve decided to abandon the initial HTML/CSS/JS file consideration.\n\n\n**Implementing the Site Layout**\n\nI\'m now diving into the component structure, using Framer Motion for revealing animations with a `SectionWrapper` component. Data will be organized in `src/data.ts`. The focus is on the basic layout and global styles via `index.css`, and a `Navbar` for consistent navigation. I\'m creating components for all sections like `Hero`, `About`, `Services`, `Projects`, etc., all ready to be strung together in `App.tsx`.\n\n\n**Planning Content Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating content and planning the animations. I\'m targeting fade-in animations for the Hero section and scroll-triggered animations for other sections, all using `framer-motion`. I\'m also preparing for the gradient styles. I\'m focusing on the component structure and using `@tailwindcss/vite`, already correctly configured, I\'ll then generate tools for file creation, and consider either a single file, or groups, rather than individual components for everything. I\'ll include the content in data.ts, and ui components into ui.tsx. I am now creating a design plan for the site.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "29xapp8v"
      name: "view_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"AbsolutePath\":\"/skills/system_skills/design_guidelines/SKILL.md\",\"toolAction\":\"Viewing design guidelines skill\",\"toolSummary\":\"Read design guidelines\"}"
