  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Dark Mode Implementation**\n\nI\'m currently focused on incorporating a dark mode toggle into the navigation bar, and I\'ve quickly realized that Tailwind v4 offers built-in dark mode detection. However, I need a manual toggle, which seems straightforward to achieve by adding the `.dark` class to the `html` tag. I\'ll need to figure out how to add the toggle in Tailwind V4.\n\n\n**Configuring Dark Mode with Tailwind**\n\nI\'m now diving into configuring Tailwind\'s dark mode. Initially, I considered using `@custom-variant` in `index.css`, and I initially tested using `@custom-variant dark (&:is(.dark *));`. The simplest method is wrapping the application, or `html` itself. So, I will move this logic to `ThemeContext.tsx`, which I am now creating to handle the theme state.\n\n\n**Implementing Theme State Logic**\n\nI\'ve just finished creating `ThemeContext.tsx`, and I\'m quite satisfied with how the logic for the theme state is shaping up. I\'m now leveraging local storage to persist the user\'s theme preference and also using `prefers-color-scheme` for initial detection. The `ThemeProvider` component handles the initial theme loading and also the theme toggle, toggling the `dark` class on the `html` element.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "cdkmeegm"
      name: "create_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Content\":\"import { createContext, useContext, useEffect, useState, ReactNode } from \\\"react\\\";\\n\\ntype Theme = \\\"light\\\" | \\\"dark\\\";\\n\\ninterface ThemeContextType {\\n  theme: Theme;\\n  toggleTheme: () => void;\\n}\\n\\nconst ThemeContext = createContext<ThemeContextType | undefined>(undefined);\\n\\nexport function ThemeProvider({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {\\n  const [theme, setTheme] = useState<Theme>(\\\"light\\\");\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    // Check localStorage first\\n    const savedTheme = localStorage.getItem(\\\"theme\\\") as Theme | null;\\n    if (savedTheme === \\\"dark\\\" || savedTheme === \\\"light\\\") {\\n      setTheme(savedTheme);\\n      document.documentElement.classList.toggle(\\\"dark\\\", savedTheme === \\\"dark\\\");\\n    } else if (window.matchMedia(\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\").matches) {\\n      // Fallback to system preference\\n      setTheme(\\\"dark\\\");\\n      document.documentElement.classList.add(\\\"dark\\\");\\n    }\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  const toggleTheme = () => {\\n    setTheme((prev) => {\\n      const newTheme = prev === \\\"light\\\" ? \\\"dark\\\" : \\\"light\\\";\\n      localStorage.setItem(\\\"theme\\\", newTheme);\\n      document.documentElement.classList.toggle(\\\"dark\\\", newTheme === \\\"dark\\\");\\n      return newTheme;\\n    });\\n  };\\n\\n  return (\\n    <ThemeContext.Provider value={{ theme, toggleTheme }}>\\n      {children}\\n    </ThemeContext.Provider>\\n  );\\n}\\n\\nexport function useTheme() {\\n  const context = useContext(ThemeContext);\\n  if (context === undefined) {\\n    throw new Error(\\\"useTheme must be used within a ThemeProvider\\\");\\n  }\\n  return context;\\n}\\n\",\"Overwrite\":true,\"TargetFile\":\"/src/context/ThemeContext.tsx\",\"toolAction\":\"Creating ThemeContext\",\"toolSummary\":\"Create ThemeContext file\"}"
