  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 1
    user_intent: "Implement Theme Switcher\nThe user wants to implement a theme switcher in the Navbar component to toggle between light and dark themes. The user\'s theme preference should be persisted using local storage."
    session_summary: "The user wants to implement a theme switcher in the Navbar component to toggle between a light and dark theme, persisting the preference using local storage.\n\nHere\'s a summary of the work done and key information:\n\n**Features Implemented:**\n\n*   **Theme Switcher:**\n    *   A `ThemeProvider` component has been created (`src/context/ThemeContext.tsx`) to manage the theme state.\n    *   It uses `useState` for the current theme (`light` or `dark`) and `useEffect` to:\n        *   Read the theme preference from `localStorage` on mount.\n        *   If no preference is found in `localStorage`, it falls back to the system\'s preferred color scheme (`window.matchMedia`).\n        *   It applies a `dark` class to the `document.documentElement` to enable dark mode styling via Tailwind CSS.\n    *   A `useTheme` hook is provided for easy access to the theme context.\n    *   The `toggleTheme` function in the context updates the theme state, saves it to `localStorage`, and toggles the `dark` class on the `document.documentElement`.\n*   **Navbar Integration:**\n    *   The `Navbar` component in `src/components/Layout.tsx` now uses the `useTheme` hook.\n    *   A theme toggle button (Moon/Sun icon) has been added to the Navbar.\n    *   Clicking the button calls `toggleTheme` to switch between themes.\n    *   Conditional Tailwind CSS classes (`dark:bg-zinc-950/80`, `dark:border-white/10`, `dark:text-zinc-50`, etc.) have been applied to the Navbar and its elements to adapt their appearance in dark mode.\n*   **App Component Integration:**\n    *   The main `App.tsx` component now wraps its content with the `ThemeProvider`.\n    *   The main `div` in `App.tsx` has been updated with `dark:` variants for background and text colors (`dark:bg-zinc-950 dark:text-zinc-50`) and a `transition-colors duration-300` class for smooth theme transitions.\n*   **Global CSS Updates:**\n    *   `src/index.css` has been updated to include:\n        *   An import for the \'Inter\' font.\n        *   A `@custom-variant dark (&:where(.dark, .dark *));` directive to enable Tailwind\'s dark mode variant.\n        *   Basic smooth scrolling and text rendering styles.\n*   **Component-Specific Dark Mode Styling:**\n    *   Dark mode styles have been applied to various components (`AnimatedSection`, `Hero`, `About`, `Services`, `Process`, `Projects`, `Contact`) using Tailwind\'s `dark:` prefix for elements like backgrounds, text colors, borders, and shadows to ensure a consistent look across both themes.\n\n**Dependencies and APIs:**\n\n*   `react`, `react-dom`, `vite`, `tailwindcss`, `@vitejs/plugin-react`, `@tailwindcss/vite` (existing)\n*   `lucide-react` (for icons like Moon, Sun, etc.)\n*   `motion/react` (for animations, not directly used for theme switching but part of the overall animation strategy)\n*   `localStorage` API (for persisting theme preference)\n*   `window.matchMedia` API (for detecting system preference)\n\n**Design Decisions:**\n\n*   **Theme Persistence:** `localStorage` is used for persistence, providing a good balance between user preference and browser compatibility.\n*   **System Preference Fallback:** The application respects the user\'s operating system preference if no explicit choice is made.\n*   **Tailwind CSS `dark:` variant:** This is the primary mechanism for applying dark mode styles, ensuring consistency with the existing utility-first approach.\n*   **Smooth Transitions:** `transition-colors duration-300` is applied to the main app container and other elements to provide a visually pleasing transition between themes.\n*   **Icon Toggling:** Moon and Sun icons are used to visually indicate the current theme and the action of toggling.\n\n**Environmental Variables:**\n\n*   No new environmental variables were introduced or modified for this feature.\n\n**Security Preferences:**\n\n*   No specific security concerns were raised or addressed in this iteration.\n\n**Special User Requests and Preferences:**\n\n*   Implement a theme switcher.\n*   Toggle between light and dark themes.\n*   Persist theme preference using `localStorage`.\n\n**Existing Blockers and Bugs:**\n\n*   None identified.\n\n**Next Steps:**\n\n*   Review all components to ensure dark mode styling is applied consistently and correctly.\n*   Test the theme switching functionality thoroughly across different browsers and devices.\n*   Consider adding more sophisticated background animations or color shifts for dark mode if desired.\n*   Potentially refactor some of the `dark:` class applications for better maintainability if the codebase grows significantly.\n\nThe current state of the application has a functional theme switcher with persistence and respects system preferences, with dark mode styling applied across most of the UI."
