    thinking: "**Addressing the Error**\n\nI\'m currently focused on addressing the unexpected error that interrupted the logo showcase. I\'m prioritizing understanding the nature of the error to figure out how to continue seamlessly with the user\'s initial request. I\'m investigating how the interruption affected my execution and am working to develop a solution. I am trying to finish the operation as requested.\n\n\n**Designing the Showcase**\n\nI\'m now designing the logo showcase; the user wants something beautiful and attractive, with hover animations. I\'m considering a scrolling marquee or an animated bento grid, given the available tools data. I\'ll create a component, likely named `ToolLogos` or `TechStack`, that uses Lucide icons or text/simple SVGs to represent the tools, since I can\'t access their actual logos. I am thinking of using styled text or pill badges for the Adobe products.\n\n\n**Implementing the Showcase**\n\nI\'m now diving into implementation details. I\'ll create a `TechStack` component in `src/components/` to build a marquee or dedicated section. The user wants me to use the tools in their skills section, so I\'ll design a generic Logo Marquee for their \"Tools & Technologies\". I\'m incorporating hover animations like pop-up effects, gradient borders, and glows for an attractive user experience.\n\n\n**Constructing the Marquee**\n\nI\'m now focused on the marquee implementation; I\'ve defined the CSS keyframes for the marquee animation. I\'ll include two rows moving in opposite directions for added visual appeal, and hover interactions to pause the animation and highlight the logo. I\'m working with simple icons or stylized badges to represent tools, and I\'ll create the CSS animation in either `index.css` or the Tailwind config.\n\n\n\n**Refining the Layout**\n\nI\'m now refining the `TechStack` component. I\'ve considered stylized text cards with blurred backgrounds, but I\'m leaning toward a masonry or marquee layout for a modern look, where I can implement a continuous marquee with CSS. I\'m focusing on the CSS to ensure a smooth, looping animation, and I\'ve started the implementation. I\'m still weighing the pros and cons of using the `motion/react` library.\n\n\n**Generating the Tech Stack**\n\nI\'m now generating the tech stack data and considering how to represent each tool visually. I\'ve decided to create an array of objects, each containing the tool\'s name and a corresponding color, like `[{ name: \"Figma\", color: \"text-pink-500\" }, ...]`. I\'ll divide the tools into two rows for the marquee effect, and double each row for a continuous animation. I\'m focusing on creating sleek glass-morphism cards with icon placeholders to represent each tool since I don\'t have SVGs. I\'m checking `lucide-react` for brand icons like Figma, Framer, and Github.\n\n\n**Visualizing the Tools**\n\nI\'m now determining the visual representation for each tool, and I\'ve established a structure for each tool object. I\'m assigning initial letter logos for each item for brands where I can\'t find an appropriate icon. I\'m using gradient backgrounds to increase the visual appeal and uniqueness of the tool badges; I\'m incorporating the tool name, icon, and colors.\n\n\n\n**Finalizing the Component**\n\nI\'m now putting the finishing touches on the `TechStack` component. I\'ve focused on representing the tool objects visually; I\'m using gradient backgrounds to give each tool badge visual appeal and uniqueness. I\'m incorporating the tool name, icon, and colors. I am now incorporating the generated array into the `TechStack` component, to be used in the markup. I\'ll insert `<TechStack />` between `Projects` and `Skills`.\n\n\n**Refining the Implementation**\n\nI\'m now refining the `TechStack` implementation. I\'ve integrated `motion/react` for smooth transitions and animations within the tool badges. I\'m focusing on the visual appeal of these badges, including gradient backgrounds, custom shadows, and dynamic color assignments for each tool based on its name. I am also working on dynamic keyframes to avoid code duplication.\n\n\n**Optimizing the Animation**\n\nI\'m now optimizing the marquee animation and focusing on the appearance of the tool cards. I\'m finalizing the data structure for the tool information, and I am incorporating a duplicated array to fill the screen. I am refining the `ToolCard` component to include the dynamic styling, and implementing it within the marquee. I am incorporating hover effects.\n\n\n\n**Adjusting the ToolCard**\n\nI\'m now making adjustments to the `ToolCard`. I am adding hover effects that have a scale transition and are dynamically assigned a tool color. I am also working on dynamic keyframes to avoid code duplication in the styles, and implementing it within the marquee.\n\n\n**Refining the Arsenal**\n\nI\'m now refining the visual presentation, focusing on the \"My Digital Arsenal\" section, which uses the marquee animation. I\'m dynamically generating the content, ensuring proper responsiveness across different viewports. I\'m focusing on the data for `ToolCard` styling, and integrating the generated data into the `TechStack` component. I am working on the marquee animation logic.\n\n\n**Implementing the Marquee**\n\nI\'ve just added the necessary CSS for the marquee animation to `index.css`, including keyframes and hover-pause functionality. I\'ve also injected the `TechStack` component into `App.tsx` and am now focusing on refining the overall design. I am trying to make the showcase a visually appealing and premium experience for the user.\n\n\n**Integrating Motion**\n\nI am now integrating `motion.div` from `framer-motion` for smoother hover effects on the tool cards, instead of pure CSS animations. I\'m focusing on refining the visual structure, including verifying imports in `TechStack.tsx`, modifying `index.css`, and modifying `App.tsx`. I\'ve created the `TechStack` component and am finalizing the content and layout. I am also considering the duplicate tools array logic.\n\n\n**Refining the Marquee**\n\nI\'m now refining the marquee logic, ensuring a seamless and visually appealing animation. I\'ve implemented the tool array duplication for continuous scrolling and the 50% translation alignment. The `TechStack` component is being structured, and I am dynamically assigning colors and icons to each tool card based on my new data structure.\n\n\n**Refining the Colors**\n\nI\'m now refining the color scheme, focusing on Adobe products. I\'ve adjusted the color assignments for Photoshop and Illustrator to `from-blue-600 to-blue-400` and `from-orange-600 to-orange-400` respectively, to match Tailwind utilities. I want to keep them consistent with their Tailwind equivalent.\n\n\n**Implementing Tailwind Colors**\n\nI\'m now implementing the new color scheme, focusing on Tailwind\'s utility classes for broader compiler support. I\'ve updated color assignments in `toolLogos` to avoid arbitrary hex values. I\'m prioritizing direct Tailwind colors such as `blue-600` and ensuring consistent styling, aiming for future-proof color implementation.\n\n\n**Validating the Utilities**\n\nI\'m now validating Tailwind utility classes for color consistency. I updated tool color assignments within the `toolLogos` array, like Elementor to `from-red-600` and Shopify to `from-emerald-600`. The Tailwind class `from-sky-800` is now confirmed as valid. I am now drafting the `TechStack` component.\n\n\n\n**Finalizing the Component**\n\nI\'m now finalizing the tool card, including logic for infinite scroll, and hover effects that enhance the user experience. I\'ve focused on seamless integration with the existing `TechStack` and the data structure. I am making final tweaks to ensure responsiveness and a polished visual presentation.\n\n\n**Adjusting the Layout**\n\nI\'m now adjusting the overall layout of the marquee component for optimal presentation. I\'m focusing on ensuring responsiveness for all viewport sizes while retaining visual appeal. I\'ve updated the tool color assignments to ensure consistency across the tool cards, and implemented them in the updated component.\n\n\n**Analyzing the Behavior**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the marquee animation to ensure seamless looping behavior; I am trying to resolve any visual hitches. I am exploring how `w-max` and `translateX(-50%)` work to create a continuous animation by duplicating the tool row. I am trying to make the tool appear seamless, like a continuous loop.\n\n\n\n**Validating the Logic**\n\nI\'m now validating the logic for seamless marquee animations using `translateX(-50%)` and duplicating the tool rows. By translating a container with four repetitions by 50%, the view at -50% is identical to 0%, creating a continuous loop. I\'ve confirmed that the CSS rules map correctly for this effect. I\'ll make sure the elements are wide enough.\n\n\n"
