  planner_response {
    response: "To add your actual logo files to the showcase, you just need to upload the images to your project and update the data file. Here is exactly how to do it:\n\n### Step 1: Upload Your Logos\n1. Open the **Files** panel on the left side of your AI Studio interface (the folder icon).\n2. Look for the `public` folder. (If it doesn\'t exist, you can create it, or simply upload files to the root).\n3. **Upload your logo images** (PNG, JPG, or SVG) into that `public` folder. \n*(Hint: You can just drag and drop the files directly from your computer into the file explorer!)*\n\n### Step 2: Update the Image Paths\nOnce your images are uploaded (for example, let\'s say you uploaded `aura-logo.png` and `nexis.svg` to the `public` folder), you will need to update the data file.\n\nGo to your `/src/data.ts` file, find the `branding` array, and change the `img` links from the default placeholder links to your new file names (starting with a `/`).\n\nHere is how it will look:\n\n```typescript\n// Inside /src/data.ts\n\n  branding: [\n    { \n      id: 1, \n      name: \"Aura Luxury\", \n      desc: \"Premium boutique visual identity\", \n      img: \"/aura-logo.png\" // <--- Change this to your uploaded file\'s name\n    },\n    { \n      id: 2, \n      name: \"Nexis Tech\", \n      desc: \"Modern IT solutions logo\", \n      img: \"/nexis.svg\" // <--- Change this to your uploaded file\'s name\n    },\n    // ... continue for the rest\n  ],\n```\n\n*(Note: Any file placed in the `public` folder can be accessed directly with a `/` in the URL).*\n\n**Want me to do it for you?** \nSimply drag and drop your logo files directly into this chat window, tell me their names along with the brand details, and I will write the code to plug them all in for you!"
    thinking: "**Clarifying the Goal**\n\nI\'m now focused on understanding the core request: incorporating user-provided logos into a new \"Branding & Logo Showcase\" block. The key is clearly how to facilitate the upload of image files.\n\n\n**Refining the Process**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the best way for a user to actually implement the logo upload process. I need to guide them, step-by-step, in the best possible method. Right now, I will be telling them they can upload their images to the AI Studio project via the file explorer or by dropping them into the chat. Then I must provide the exact code to modify in `src/data.ts` to integrate the images.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "To add your actual logo files to the showcase, you just need to upload the images to your project and update the data file. Here is exactly how to do it:\n\n### Step 1: Upload Your Logos\n1. Open the **Files** panel on the left side of your AI Studio interface (the folder icon).\n2. Look for the `public` folder. (If it doesn\'t exist, you can create it, or simply upload files to the root).\n3. **Upload your logo images** (PNG, JPG, or SVG) into that `public` folder. \n*(Hint: You can just drag and drop the files directly from your computer into the file explorer!)*\n\n### Step 2: Update the Image Paths\nOnce your images are uploaded (for example, let\'s say you uploaded `aura-logo.png` and `nexis.svg` to the `public` folder), you will need to update the data file.\n\nGo to your `/src/data.ts` file, find the `branding` array, and change the `img` links from the default placeholder links to your new file names (starting with a `/`).\n\nHere is how it will look:\n\n```typescript\n// Inside /src/data.ts\n\n  branding: [\n    { \n      id: 1, \n      name: \"Aura Luxury\", \n      desc: \"Premium boutique visual identity\", \n      img: \"/aura-logo.png\" // <--- Change this to your uploaded file\'s name\n    },\n    { \n      id: 2, \n      name: \"Nexis Tech\", \n      desc: \"Modern IT solutions logo\", \n      img: \"/nexis.svg\" // <--- Change this to your uploaded file\'s name\n    },\n    // ... continue for the rest\n  ],\n```\n\n*(Note: Any file placed in the `public` folder can be accessed directly with a `/` in the URL).*\n\n**Want me to do it for you?** \nSimply drag and drop your logo files directly into this chat window, tell me their names along with the brand details, and I will write the code to plug them all in for you!"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 83142108
    }
