  planner_response {
    response: "Got it! Since you want to handle the images yourself and skip the overlay names, I have completely refactored the UI logic to support \"nameless\" logos perfectly.\n\nHere\'s what I changed to make your workflow frictionless:\n\n1. **Made Text UI Overlays 100% Optional:** The interface intelligence will now detect whether a name/description exists. If you leave them completely blank, the text overlays, shadow blocks, and dark gradients on hover *won\'t* render at all, leaving you with a visually clean card displaying exactly just your pure artwork.\n2. **Simplified The Main Grid:** With just pure images, the grid cards will still light up with the Emerald gradient glow on hover, gently scale outwards to `105%` size, flip off grayscale bounds, and present the magnifying glass UI in the corner. \n3. **Empty Source Template:** Inside `/src/data.ts`, I cleared all placeholder brand names, so each entry literally just looks like `{ id: 1, name: \"\", desc: \"\", img: \"url\" }` now. \n\n### What You Should Do Now:\n1. Re-upload your logos inside the `public` folder (it\'s best to upload to the `public/` folder so Vite serves them correctly natively to the frontend root).\n2. Go into the `/src/data.ts` file right now and quickly paste your file names into the `img: \"\"` strings (e.g. `img: \"/Asset 20.png\"`, `img: \"/Logo.png\"`). \n\nIt will instantly render them on the UI with full animations with zero text!"
    modified_response: "Got it! Since you want to handle the images yourself and skip the overlay names, I have completely refactored the UI logic to support \"nameless\" logos perfectly.\n\nHere\'s what I changed to make your workflow frictionless:\n\n1. **Made Text UI Overlays 100% Optional:** The interface intelligence will now detect whether a name/description exists. If you leave them completely blank, the text overlays, shadow blocks, and dark gradients on hover *won\'t* render at all, leaving you with a visually clean card displaying exactly just your pure artwork.\n2. **Simplified The Main Grid:** With just pure images, the grid cards will still light up with the Emerald gradient glow on hover, gently scale outwards to `105%` size, flip off grayscale bounds, and present the magnifying glass UI in the corner. \n3. **Empty Source Template:** Inside `/src/data.ts`, I cleared all placeholder brand names, so each entry literally just looks like `{ id: 1, name: \"\", desc: \"\", img: \"url\" }` now. \n\n### What You Should Do Now:\n1. Re-upload your logos inside the `public` folder (it\'s best to upload to the `public/` folder so Vite serves them correctly natively to the frontend root).\n2. Go into the `/src/data.ts` file right now and quickly paste your file names into the `img: \"\"` strings (e.g. `img: \"/Asset 20.png\"`, `img: \"/Logo.png\"`). \n\nIt will instantly render them on the UI with full animations with zero text!"
